# Drafted by Gemini (side quests act 2 batch 1: quack), edited.

~ orla_start
Narrator: Propped among the cots in the taproom, a tiny old woman taps a knuckle against her knee in strict time.
granny_orla_pike [angry]: Keep your boots still by my blankets. The fevered ones need a straight tune to sleep, and this room is full of folks breathing off-key.
* Ask her to sing -> orla_sing
* Offer to sing yourself -> orla_judge
* Leave -> END

~ orla_sing
granny_orla_pike [sly]: Am I a clockwork lark to pipe up whenever a stranger rattles the latch? Give me a verse first, so I hear whether you have a throat or a rusted hinge.
-> orla_start

~ orla_judge
Narrator: You clear your throat and offer a low moorland air while the sickroom grows quiet.
granny_orla_pike [weary]: Flat on the turn, rushed at the cadence, and you swallowed the third word. Listen here, you hopeless magpie, it goes like this.
Narrator: She hums the same verse back through toothless gums, rich and steady as hearth smoke.
set orla_sang
-> orla_start
